    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In thesaurus-based query expansion technique, for every term t in a query, we expand the query using the synonyms and related words of t taken from the thesaurus. This can increase ( ). \n\nOptions: \nA. precision\nB. recall\nC. performance\nD. mean average precision\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**B**\n\nThesaurus-based query expansion adds synonyms and related terms, broadening the query to retrieve more potentially relevant documents, which primarily increases recall (the fraction of relevant documents retrieved). While it may decrease precision (relevance of retrieved documents) due to added noise, recall is the key benefit. Performance and mean average precision are not directly targeted by this technique.\n\n\\boxed{B}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe provided answer identifies B (recall) as correct because thesaurus-based query expansion adds synonyms and related terms to the query, broadening its scope to match more documents, including those with relevant content not captured by the original terms. This directly enhances recall, defined as the proportion of relevant documents retrieved from the total relevant documents available. In contrast, precision measures the relevance of retrieved documents and may decline due to irrelevant matches; performance is ambiguous and not the primary focus; mean average precision combines both metrics but is not specifically increased by expansion.",
