      "generated_answer": "```python\ncomp = []\ni = 0\nn = len(word)\nwhile i < n:\n    c = word[i]\n    j = i + 1\n    while j < n and word[j] == c and j - i < 9:\n        j += 1\n    length = j - i\n    comp.append(str(length))\n    comp.append(c)\n    i = j\nreturn ''.join(comp)\n```\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe provided function body implements the compression algorithm efficiently in O(N) time, where N is the length of the input string.\n\n- Initialize an empty list `comp` to collect parts of the result, and set index `i` to 0 to track the current position in `word`.\n- Use `n = len(word)` for quick length access.\n- In the main while loop (`while i < n`):\n  - Identify the current character `c = word[i]`.\n  - Advance index `j` starting from `i + 1`, incrementing `j` as long as `word[j]` matches `c` and the run length (`j - i`) remains less than 9.\n  - This ensures the prefix is the maximum length of repeating `c` up to 9 characters.\n  - Compute the prefix length as `length = j - i`.\n  - Append `str(length)` and `c` to `comp`.\n  - Update `i` to `j` to process the next segment.\n- After the loop, join the list into a string with `''.join(comp)` and return it.\n\nThis approach processes each character exactly once, handling cases like long runs (split into chunks ≤9), single characters, or mixed sequences as per the examples.",
