      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    next_node = [0] + [int(x) for x in data[1:1 + N]]\n    \n    def find_cycle(start):\n        # Floyd's cycle detection to find a meeting point\n        tort = start\n        hare = start\n        while True:\n            tort = next_node[tort]\n            hare = next_node[next_node[hare]]\n            if tort == hare:\n                break\n        # Find the start of the cycle\n        tort = start\n        while tort != hare:\n            tort = next_node[tort]\n            hare = next_node[hare]\n        cycle_start = tort\n        # Build the cycle list\n        cycle = [cycle_start]\n        cur = next_node[cycle_start]\n        while cur != cycle_start:\n            cycle.append(cur)\n            cur = next_node[cur]\n        return cycle\n    \n    cycle = find_cycle(1)\n    print(len(cycle))\n    print(' '.join(map(str, cycle)))\n\nsolve()\n```",
