    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef inv_count(perm):\n    n = len(perm)\n    cnt = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if perm[i] > perm[j]:\n                cnt += 1\n    return cnt\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    H = int(data[idx])\n    W = int(data[idx + 1])\n    idx += 2\n\n    A = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        row = [int(data[idx + j]) for j in range(W)]\n        A.append(row)\n        idx += W\n\n    B = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        row = [int(data[idx + j]) for j in range(W)]\n        B.append(row)\n        idx += W\n\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    for prow in permutations(range(H)):\n        for pcol in permutations(range(W)):\n            match = True\n            for i in range(H):\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if A[prow[i]][pcol[j]] != B[i][j]:\n                        match = False\n                        break\n                if not match:\n                    break\n            if match:\n                cost = inv_count(prow) + inv_count(pcol)\n                if cost < min_cost:\n                    min_cost = cost\n\n    if min_cost == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_cost)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
