      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport bisect\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef min_moves(nums: List[int], k: int, maxChanges: int) -> int:\n    n = len(nums)\n    ones = [i for i in range(n) if nums[i] == 1]\n    t = len(ones)\n    prefix_ones = [0] * (t + 1)\n    for j in range(t):\n        prefix_ones[j + 1] = prefix_ones[j] + ones[j]\n    \n    base = max(0, k - maxChanges)\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    \n    for pos in range(n):\n        l = max(0, pos - 2)\n        r = min(n - 1, pos + 2)\n        local_costs = [abs(i - pos) for i in range(l, r + 1) if nums[i] == 1]\n        local_total = len(local_costs)\n        sum_local = sum(local_costs)\n        \n        if k <= local_total:\n            sorted_local = sorted(local_costs)\n            this_cost = sum(sorted_local[:k])\n        elif k - local_total <= maxChanges:\n            this_cost = sum_local + 2 * (k - local_total)\n        else:\n            # compute sum of smallest base dists\n            idx = bisect.bisect_left(ones, pos)\n            L = idx\n            R = t - idx\n            lo = max(0, base - R)\n            hi = min(L, base)\n            best = -1\n            while lo <= hi:\n                mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n                if mid == 0:\n                    dl = float('-inf')\n                else:\n                    dl = pos - ones[idx - mid]\n                ar = base - mid\n                if ar == 0:\n                    dr = float('-inf')\n                else:\n                    dr = ones[idx + ar - 1] - pos\n                if dl <= dr:\n                    best = mid\n                    lo = mid + 1\n                else:\n                    hi = mid - 1\n            al = best\n            ar = base - al\n            sum_dist_left = 0\n            if al > 0:\n                sum_pos_left = prefix_ones[idx] - prefix_ones[idx - al]\n                sum_dist_left = al * pos - sum_pos_left\n            sum_dist_right = 0\n            if ar > 0:\n                sum_pos_right = prefix_ones[idx + ar] - prefix_ones[idx]\n                sum_dist_right = sum_pos_right - ar * pos\n            sum_base = sum_dist_left + sum_dist_right\n            this_cost = sum_base + 2 * maxChanges\n        \n        if this_cost < min_cost:\n            min_cost = this_cost\n    \n    return int(min_cost)\n```\nThe function body is the code above without the `def` line and return type annotation, but since it's the executable function, this is it.\n\nWait, the prompt: \"Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution.\"\n\nSo, the body is the content inside the def.",
