      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    line = 0\n    first = data[line].split()\n    H = int(first[0])\n    W = int(first[1])\n    N = int(first[2])\n    line += 1\n    T = data[line]\n    line += 1\n    grid = data[line:line + H]\n    moves = {'L': 'R', 'R': 'L', 'U': 'D', 'D': 'U'}\n    delta = {'L': (0, -1), 'R': (0, 1), 'U': (-1, 0), 'D': (1, 0)}\n    rev_moves = [moves[T[i]] for i in range(N - 1, -1, -1)]\n    count = 0\n    for r in range(H):\n        row = grid[r]\n        for c in range(W):\n            if row[c] != '.':\n                continue\n            cr = r\n            cc = c\n            valid = True\n            for rm in rev_moves:\n                dr, dc = delta[rm]\n                cr += dr\n                cc += dc\n                if cr < 0 or cr >= H or cc < 0 or cc >= W or grid[cr][cc] != '.':\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid:\n                count += 1\n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
