    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9180",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain and discuss why the branch and link register (BALR) instruction is usually one of the most important instruc-tions of the IBM/360-370 computers?\n\nOptions: \nA. BALR instruction is important because it is used for data encryption and security purposes.\nB. BALR instruction is important because it increases the graphical processing capabilities of the computer.\nC. BALR instruction is important because it directly manipulates arithmetic operations.\nD. BALR instruction is important because it simplifies the programming process.\nE. BALR instruction is important because it serves as a primary instruction for input/output operations.\nF. BALR instruction is important because it speeds up the program.\nG. BALR instruction is important because it allows for base address loading into the base register of the program, which is crucial for the program's execution.\nH. BALR instruction is important because it enables the computer to perform multitasking more efficiently.\nI. BALR instruction is important because it allows for immediate value assignment to multiple registers.\nJ. BALR instruction is important because it reduces memory usage.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**G**\n\nBALR (Branch and Link Register) is crucial in IBM System/360-370 because it loads the address of the next instruction into a specified register (e.g., BALR 12,0 sets base register 12 to the current program counter), enabling base-displacement addressing vital for program execution. Without it, establishing base registers for memory addressing would be cumbersome in this architecture lacking direct PC-relative or immediate load address instructions. This makes BALR foundational for linking, subroutines, and overall program structure.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
