    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9238",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| The softmax function is commonly used in mutliclass logistic regression. Statement 2| The temperature of a nonuniform softmax distribution affects its entropy.\n\nOptions: \nA. False, False\nB. True, Statement 2 is not related to Statement 1\nC. False, Both statements are related to each other\nD. Statement 2 is true, but Statement 1 is irrelevant\nE. Statement 1 is true, but Statement 2 is irrelevant\nF. False, True\nG. True, False\nH. True, Both statements are unrelated to each other\nI. False, Statement 1 is not related to Statement 2\nJ. True, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**Both statements are true.**  \nStatement 1 is correct because softmax converts logits to probabilities in multiclass logistic regression.  \nStatement 2 is correct because temperature scales the logits in softmax, altering the distribution's peakedness and thus its entropy for nonuniform cases.  \n\n\\boxed{J}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning evaluates each statement independently for truthfulness before matching to options.\n\nStatement 1 is true, as the softmax function standardly converts raw scores (logits) into a probability distribution summing to 1, which is the core mechanism in multiclass logistic regression.\n\nStatement 2 is true, since temperature in the softmax formula—exp(logit_i / T) / sum(exp(logit_j / T))—controls the distribution's sharpness; for nonuniform logits (not all equal), lowering T decreases entropy by making it more peaked, while raising T increases entropy toward uniformity.\n\nWith both statements verified as true, option J (\"True, True\") is the precise match among the choices.",
