    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nAccording to Joseph Butler's moral philosophy in his *Sermons*, conscience necessarily approves virtuous (good) actions, making it impossible to perform a good action without that approval. This contrasts with vice, which conscience disapproves but which people can still commit despite the internal conflict. Option I is incorrect because Butler acknowledges that actions against conscience (evil) are possible, albeit painful.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
