    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Parfit, both Taurek and Lewis assume that for there to be a “sum of pain,” it must be:\n\nOptions: \nA. all be avoidable.\nB. only felt by multiple people at different times.\nC. all be experienced in the same way.\nD. all be of the same intensity.\nE. all felt by a single person.\nF. all be caused by a single source.\nG. all be caused by multiple sources.\nH. all be caused by a single event.\nI. all felt at a single time.\nJ. all of the above.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
