      "generated_answer": "**C**\n\nMasking is a well-established psychoacoustic phenomenon where one sound obscures another, particularly when they share similar frequencies or intensities. In an orchestra, lower-frequency instruments (e.g., cellos, bassoons) can mask higher-frequency ones (e.g., violins, flutes), so musicians dynamically adjust dynamics and timbre to ensure balance. Option C accurately describes this without conflating it with unrelated concepts like physical barriers or visual effects.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
