      "generated_answer": "**D**\n\nThe skewness coefficient is calculated using the formula \\(\\gamma_1 = \\frac{m_3}{m_2^{3/2}}\\), where \\(m_3 = -149.04\\) and \\(m_2 = 48.6\\), yielding \\(\\gamma_1 \\approx -0.44\\). The mean is 66.5, and the deviations from the midpoints facilitate precise computation of the moments. This matches option D among the given choices.\n\n\\boxed{D}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by identifying the skewness formula for grouped data: \\(\\gamma_1 = \\frac{m_3}{m_2^{3/2}}\\), where \\(m_3\\) and \\(m_2\\) are the third and second central moments. Total frequency \\(n = 100\\), and the mean \\(\\bar{x} = \\sum f_i x_i / n = 6650 / 100 = 66.5\\). Deviations from the mean are -15, -9, -3, 3, and 9 for the midpoints; then, \\(\\sum f_i (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = 4860\\), so \\(m_2 = 48.6\\); and \\(\\sum f_i (x_i - \\bar{x})^3 = -14904\\), so \\(m_3 = -149.04\\). Finally, \\(m_2^{3/2} = 48.6 \\times \\sqrt{48.6} \\approx 338.88\\), yielding \\(\\gamma_1 = -149.04 / 338.88 \\approx -0.44\\), which corresponds to option D.",
