    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_4",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Some of key differences between Islamic finance and conventional finance include - prohibition of charging and paying _______, prohibition on ______ and ______ transactions, prohibition of sinful investment and requirement for all financial products to be backed by __________.\n\nOptions: \nA. Interest, Certain, Assured, Both tangible and intangible assets\nB. Interest, Uncertain, Assured, Both tangible and intangible assets\nC. Interest, Uncertain, Speculative, Intangible assets\nD. Interest, Certain, Assured, Tangible assets\nE. Interest, Uncertain, Assured, Intangible assets\nF. Profit, Uncertain, Speculative, Tangible assets\nG. Interest, Uncertain, Speculative, Tangible assets\nH. Interest, Certain, Speculative, Intangible assets\nI. Profit, Certain, Assured, Tangible assets\nJ. Interest, Certain, Speculative, Both tangible and intangible assets\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**G**\n\nIslamic finance prohibits riba (interest), gharar (uncertain transactions), and maysir (speculative transactions), while requiring products to be backed by tangible assets. Option G matches these precisely: Interest, Uncertain, Speculative, Tangible assets. Other options mismatch on uncertainty/speculation or asset backing.\n\n\\boxed{G}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process begins by identifying the first blank as \"interest,\" corresponding to riba, which eliminates options F and I that use \"Profit.\" Next, the second and third blanks refer to gharar (uncertain transactions) and maysir (speculative transactions), narrowing options to C and G, which specify \"Uncertain, Speculative.\" Finally, the last blank requires \"Tangible assets\" for asset-backed products, confirming G as the match, while C incorrectly uses \"Intangible assets.\" This step-by-step elimination ensures G aligns with all key principles of Islamic finance.",
