  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_727",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Record the maturity date for a draft dated (a) November 12 and payable 60 days after date, (b) June 10 and payable 3 months after date, (c) March 3 and payable 30 days after sight if it is accepted March 15, and (d) October 4 and payable 6 months after sight if it is acceptedOctober 25.\n\nOptions: \nA. January 12, September 10, April 14, April 26\nB. January 12, September 8, April 14, April 23\nC. January 10, September 11, April 15, April 26\nD. January 12, September 9, April 13, April 24\nE. January 11, September 12, April 15, April 26\nF. January 13, September 10, April 16, April 27\nG. January 11, September 11, April 13, April 24\nH. January 10, September 9, April 15, April 25\nI. January 13, September 12, April 16, April 27\nJ. January 11, September 10, April 14, April 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**J**\n\nThe maturity dates are calculated excluding the starting date and counting forward: (a) November 12 + 60 days = January 11; (b) June 10 + 3 months = September 10; (c) accepted March 15 + 30 days after sight = April 14; (d) accepted October 25 + 6 months after sight = April 25. These match option J precisely per standard negotiable instrument rules.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 316,
        "output_tokens": 98,
        "total_tokens": 2548
