    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_433",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: assume you are Indonesian. In 2010, the rupiah exchange rate was around IDR15,000/USD, and the consumer price index in Indonesia and the United States was at 100. In 2019, the exchange rate changed to IDR14,000/USD. Simultaneously, Indonesia’s inflation rose 5% due to the consumer price index rising to 105. Meanwhile, the United States’ inflation rate rose 10% due to the consumer price index rising to 110. Whats the real exchange rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 14000.00\nB. 15500.00\nC. 15000.00\nD. 16000.00\nE. 13500.00\nF. 14666.67\nG. 13888.89\nH. 14800.00\nI. 15200.00\nJ. 13333.33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**F**\n\nThe real exchange rate is calculated as the 2019 nominal rate adjusted for relative price levels: 14,000 × (110 / 105) = 14,000 × (22/21) ≈ 14,666.67.  \nThis uses the standard formula where real exchange rate = nominal (IDR/USD) × (US CPI / Indonesia CPI).  \nThe result matches option F exactly.\n\n\\boxed{F}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by identifying the formula for the real exchange rate, which adjusts the nominal exchange rate for relative inflation: real exchange rate = nominal exchange rate × (foreign CPI / home CPI), where home is Indonesia (CPI 105) and foreign is the US (CPI 110).  \nNext, substitute the 2019 values: 14,000 × (110 / 105).  \nSimplify 110 / 105 to 22/21 ≈ 1.047619, then compute 14,000 × (22/21) = (14,000 / 21) × 22 ≈ 666.6667 × 22 = 14,666.67, matching option F.  \nThis confirms the rupiah's real appreciation due to the nominal strengthening and higher US inflation.",
