    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**D**\n\nThe expected rate of return is calculated using the CAPM formula: Risk-Free Rate + Beta × (Market Return - Risk-Free Rate). Here, Risk-Free Rate = 2.8%, Beta = 1.4, and Market Return = 8.6% (historical data provided for the stock market proxy). Thus, 2.8 + 1.4 × (8.6 - 2.8) = 2.8 + 1.4 × 5.8 = 2.8 + 8.12 = 10.92%.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
