    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**C**\n\nThe portfolio's actual return is ($60,000 - $50,000)/$50,000 = 0.20.  \nExpected return via CAPM is 0.04 + 1.8*(0.12 - 0.04) = 0.04 + 0.144 = 0.184.  \nAbnormal return is 0.20 - 0.184 = 0.016.\n\n\\boxed{C}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning follows the standard formula for abnormal return, defined as the actual portfolio return minus the expected return from the Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM). First, calculate the actual return as (ending value - beginning value) / beginning value = ($60,000 - $50,000) / $50,000 = 0.20. Next, compute the expected return using CAPM: Rf + Beta × (Rm - Rf) = 0.04 + 1.8 × (0.12 - 0.04) = 0.04 + 1.8 × 0.08 = 0.04 + 0.144 = 0.184. Subtract to find abnormal return: 0.20 - 0.184 = 0.016, matching option C.",
