    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_17",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: George is seen to place an even-money $100,000 bet on the Bulls to win the NBA Finals. If George has a logarithmic utility-of-wealth function and if his current wealth is $1,000,000, what must he believe is the minimum probability that the Bulls will win?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.525\nB. 0.800\nC. 0.450\nD. 0.575\nE. 0.750\nF. 0.350\nG. 0.650\nH. 0.300\nI. 0.700\nJ. 0.400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A\n\nFor logarithmic utility, George is indifferent to the bet when \\( p \\ln(1{,}100{,}000) + (1-p) \\ln(900{,}000) = \\ln(1{,}000{,}000) \\), which simplifies to \\( p = \\frac{\\ln(1/0.9)}{\\ln(1.1/0.9)} \\approx 0.525 \\). He places the bet only if his believed \\( p \\) is at least this value.  \n\\boxed{A}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by recognizing that for a risk-averse individual with logarithmic utility, George places the bet only if the expected utility of betting equals or exceeds the utility of his current wealth at the indifference point. With current wealth \\( W = 1{,}000{,}000 \\), a win yields \\( W + 100{,}000 = 1{,}100{,}000 \\), and a loss yields \\( W - 100{,}000 = 900{,}000 \\). The indifference condition is thus \\( p \\cdot \\ln(1{,}100{,}000) + (1-p) \\cdot \\ln(900{,}000) = \\ln(1{,}000{,}000) \\).\n\nRearranging gives \\( p = \\frac{\\ln(1{,}000{,}000 / 900{,}000)}{\\ln(1{,}100{,}000 / 900{,}000)} = \\frac{\\ln(1 / 0.9)}{\\ln(1.1 / 0.9)} \\). Numerically, \\( \\ln(1 / 0.9) \\approx 0.10536 \\) and \\( \\ln(1.1 / 0.9) \\approx 0.20067 \\), so \\( p \\approx 0.10536 / 0.20067 = 0.525 \\).\n\nThis value matches option A, confirming it as the minimum probability George must believe for the Bulls to win to justify the bet.",
