      "generated_answer": "**B**\n\nThe expected utility is the average of \\(U(80000)\\), \\(U(90000)\\), ..., \\(U(140000)\\), which is approximately 18.153. The certainty equivalent is \\((18.153)^4 \\approx 108610\\). This matches option B most closely.\n\n\\boxed{B}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by identifying the certainty equivalent as the guaranteed salary CE that equals the expected utility of the job offer, where utility is \\(U(x) = x^{1/4}\\). The possible salaries are 80,000, 90,000, 100,000, 110,000, 120,000, 130,000, and 140,000, each with probability \\(1/7\\). Compute the fourth roots: approximately 16.82, 17.32, 17.78, 18.21, 18.61, 18.99, and 19.34; their sum is about 127.07, so expected utility EU ≈ 127.07 / 7 ≈ 18.153. Then, CE = (EU)^4 ≈ (18.153)^2 ≈ 329.53, and 329.53^2 ≈ 108,610, which aligns with option B as the closest match.",
