      "generated_answer": "**D**\n\nRoute A (15 miles): construction $90,000; 8% interest = $7,200; 3% taxes = $2,700; maintenance $30,000; total ≈ $40,000.  \nRoute B (5-mile underwater): construction $155,000; interest $12,400; taxes $4,650; maintenance $2,000; total ≈ $20,000.  \nSalvage values are irrelevant for first-year costs.\n\n\\boxed{D}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning identifies the first-year annual costs for each route as the sum of maintenance, taxes (3% of total construction costs), and interest (8% of total construction costs). For Route A, total construction cost is 15 miles × $6,000/mile = $90,000; taxes = 0.03 × $90,000 = $2,700; interest = 0.08 × $90,000 = $7,200; maintenance = 15 × $2,000 = $30,000; total ≈ $39,900, rounded to $40,000. For Route B, interpreted as a 5-mile underwater line, total construction cost is 5 miles × $31,000/mile = $155,000; taxes = 0.03 × $155,000 = $4,650; interest = 0.08 × $155,000 = $12,400; maintenance = 5 × $400 = $2,000; total ≈ $19,050, rounded to $20,000. These values match option D exactly, confirming it as the correct choice, with salvage values excluded as they apply after 15 years.",
