      "generated_answer": "Schedule (1): $8,000 + 1% of $80,000 = $8,000 + $800 = $8,800.  \nSchedule (2): $5,800 + 5% of ($80,000 - $30,000) = $5,800 + $2,500 = $8,300.  \nSchedule (1) is better by $500.\n\n\\boxed{H}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning evaluates the earnings for each pay schedule using the estimated $80,000 sales figure. For Schedule (1), earnings are calculated as $8,000 salary plus 1% of $80,000, which equals $800 commission, totaling $8,800. For Schedule (2), earnings are $5,800 salary plus 5% of sales exceeding $30,000 ($50,000), which is $2,500 commission, totaling $8,300. The difference is $8,800 minus $8,300 equals $500, confirming Schedule (1) is better by that amount, matching option H.",
