    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_560",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $P(r,t,T)$ denote the price at time $t$ of $1 to be paid with certainty at time $T, t\\leT$, if the short rate at time $t$ is equal to $r$. For a Vasicek model you are given: $P(0.04, 0, 2)=0.9445$, $P(0.05, 1, 3)=0.9321$, $P(r^*, 2, 4)=0.8960$. What is $r^*$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.11\nB. 0.06\nC. 0.05\nD. 0.04\nE. 0.08\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.07\nH. 0.09\nI. 0.10\nJ. 0.03\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nIn the Vasicek model, which is time-homogeneous, the 2-year bond price satisfies $\\ln P(r,2) = A - B r$. Using the points $(r=0.04, \\ln P \\approx -0.0571)$ and $(r=0.05, \\ln P \\approx -0.0703)$, $B \\approx 1.322$. For $\\ln P(0.8960,2) \\approx -0.1098$, $r^* \\approx 0.04 + ( -0.0571 - (-0.1098) ) / 1.322 \\approx 0.08$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
