    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_325",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Debra Cole wishes to buy a used car worth $720. She can either pay for the car on the installment plan, with 10% down and 12 monthly payments of $65, or borrow the $720 for the same 12 month period at 8% interest. Which method of financing is more economical? By how much?\n\nOptions: \nA. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $30\nB. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $74.40\nC. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $50\nD. Pay on the installment plan with no savings\nE. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $50\nF. Borrow the $720 with no savings\nG. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $30\nH. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $74.40\nI. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with no savings\nJ. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**H**\n\nThe installment plan costs $72 down + 12 × $65 = $852 total.  \nBorrowing $720 at 8% simple annual interest costs $720 + ($720 × 0.08) = $777.60 total.  \nBorrowing saves $852 - $777.60 = $74.40.\n\n\\boxed{H}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by calculating the total cost of the installment plan: 10% down payment on $720 is $72, plus 12 monthly payments of $65 each totaling $780, for a combined cost of $852.  \n\nNext, the cost of borrowing $720 at 8% simple annual interest for 12 months (1 year) is computed as principal plus interest: $720 + ($720 × 0.08) = $720 + $57.60 = $777.60.  \n\nFinally, the difference is $852 - $777.60 = $74.40, confirming borrowing is more economical by this amount, which matches option H.",
