    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_421",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although corporate profit maximization is not directly prescribed by major normative theories to which normative theory is it most similar?\n\nOptions: \nA. ethics of care\nB. preference utilitarianism\nC. Egoism\nD. Deontology\nE. Relativism\nF. The Categorical Imperative\nG. Virtue ethics\nH. Contractarianism\nI. hedonistic utilitarianism\nJ. Consequentialism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**C**\n\nCorporate profit maximization prioritizes self-interest (e.g., shareholders' wealth), aligning most closely with egoism among the options. Other theories like utilitarianism or consequentialism focus on broader outcomes, while deontology and virtue ethics emphasize duties or character.  \n\\boxed{C}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process begins by analyzing the question: corporate profit maximization, which prioritizes a company's or shareholders' self-interest, must be matched to the most similar normative theory among the options. Normative theories are then evaluated: ethics of care emphasizes relationships; preference utilitarianism and hedonistic utilitarianism seek overall preference satisfaction or pleasure; deontology and the Categorical Imperative focus on duties and universal rules; relativism varies by context; virtue ethics centers on character; contractarianism relies on agreements; and consequentialism broadly judges by outcomes. Profit maximization specifically resembles egoism, as it promotes acting in one's own (or the entity's) self-interest, akin to ethical egoism in business contexts like shareholder theory. Thus, egoism is selected as the closest match, distinguishing it from broader or non-self-interested theories.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 138,
        "output_tokens": 223,
        "total_tokens": 818
      },
      "provider": "azure",
