    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5855",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The cabbages you grow in your summer garden are\n\nOptions: \nA. not counted in either GDP or NDP.\nB. not counted in GDP.\nC. counted in GDP under I.\nD. counted in GDP under X-M.\nE. counted in GDP under G.\nF. counted in GDP under NX.\nG. counted in GDP under C.\nH. counted in NDP but not GDP.\nI. counted in GDP but not NDP.\nJ. counted in both GDP and NDP.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nHome-grown cabbages for personal use represent non-market household production, which is excluded from GDP (and thus NDP) as GDP only includes market transactions or imputed values for specific items like housing. Options like C, G, I, or NX incorrectly suggest inclusion under GDP components. NDP derives from GDP minus depreciation, so exclusion from GDP means exclusion from NDP.\n\n\\boxed{A}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe provided answer identifies option A as correct because home-grown cabbages for personal consumption qualify as non-market household production, which national accounts exclude from GDP. GDP measures only the market value of final goods and services, such as purchased items, while NDP is calculated as GDP minus depreciation, inheriting the same exclusions. Thus, these cabbages are not counted in either GDP or NDP, eliminating options suggesting inclusion under components like C (consumption), G (government spending), I (investment), NX (net exports), or scenarios in H, I, or J.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 154,
        "output_tokens": 195,
        "total_tokens": 695
      },
      "provider": "azure",
      "error": null
