    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by recalling the standard definition of a white noise process: a sequence of uncorrelated random variables with zero mean and constant variance. Each statement is evaluated as follows: (i) holds true, as white noise has zero mean; (ii) is correct due to constant variance; (iii) is incorrect because autocovariances are zero for all non-zero lags and equal to the variance only at lag zero, not constant across lags; (iv) is accurate, matching the uncorrelated property. Thus, only (i), (ii), and (iv) are valid, corresponding to option H.",
