      "generated_answer": "**J.** A perfectly vertical supply curve represents perfectly inelastic supply, where quantity supplied is fixed at one unit regardless of price, illustrating the unique original copy.  \nOther options describe elastic or normal curves, or unrelated concepts like the invisible hand.\n\n\\boxed{J}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe scenario involves a single, unique original signed copy of The Wealth of Nations, indicating a fixed supply that cannot increase regardless of price, which defines perfectly inelastic supply. A perfectly vertical supply curve depicts this, as it shows quantity supplied remaining constant at one unit. Among the options, J matches this description, while others represent elastic, sloping, or unrelated economic concepts.",
