    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5681",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do property rights have to do with growth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Property rights hinder economic growth.\nB. Property rights lead to an unequal distribution of wealth, which in turn stifles economic growth.\nC. Property rights are solely important for intellectual property and do not affect other types of investments.\nD. Property rights have no influence on growth.\nE. Property rights are unrelated to private investment.\nF. Property rights reduce the incentive for innovation, slowing down economic growth.\nG. Secure property rights induce people to invest, contributing to economic growth.\nH. Property rights are a concept of the past and have been replaced by new economic growth models.\nI. Property rights only benefit large corporations, not overall economic growth.\nJ. Property rights are only relevant in agricultural sectors and have no impact on urban development.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
