    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**G**\n\nSecure property rights encourage individuals and businesses to invest in assets, knowing they can reap the benefits, which drives productivity and economic growth. This is a foundational concept in economic theory, as seen in works by economists like Douglass North. Other options contradict this established relationship.\n\n\\boxed{G}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process starts by recognizing the question as an economic inquiry into the role of property rights in growth, drawing from established theory. It identifies that secure property rights reduce risks of expropriation, incentivizing private investment, innovation, and productivity, which directly fosters economic growth. Options are then systematically evaluated: A, B, F, and I misrepresent this positive link; C, E, J limit scope incorrectly; D and H deny relevance; while G precisely captures the mechanism, making it the most accurate choice based on economic consensus.",
