      "generated_answer": "G\n\nModern economists recognize issues like the principal-agent problem and separation of ownership and control in large corporations, which undermine the reliability of self-interest driving efficiency as it did for Adam Smith's independent businessmen. Option G best captures this shift, as self-interest alone is no longer sufficient without additional mechanisms like incentives or regulation. Other options either overstate (A, D), misstate (B, C, E, F), or contradict mainstream economic analysis.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
