      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nThis reflects the fundamental pacta tertiis nec nocent nec prosunt rule in Article 34 of the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties, stating that treaties neither bind (create obligations for) nor benefit (create rights for) third states without their consent. While Articles 35–36 allow obligations or rights with express or implied consent, option A precisely captures the default position. Other options either contradict this or misstate exceptions.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
