    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1052",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is it called when a remainder in the grantor's heirs is invalid and becomes a reversion in the grantor?\n\nOptions: \nA. Related Doctrine of Merger\nB. Contingent remainder\nC. Doctrine of Worthier Title\nD. Doctrine of Escheat\nE. Vested remainder\nF. Rule in Wild's Case\nG. Doctrine of Lapse\nH. Rule in Shelley's Case\nI. Doctrine of Advowson\nJ. Rule Against Perpetuities\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
