      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe proposal to authorize new preferred stock with redemption rights senior to the existing preferred stock constitutes an amendment to the certificate of incorporation under laws like DGCL §242(b)(2), which requires approval by a majority of the outstanding shares of the affected class—in this case, the existing preferred stock—due to its senior distribution rights. The existing preferred stock has 1,000 shares outstanding, but only 400 voted in favor, failing to meet the majority threshold of over 500 shares. Thus, the proposal lacks the necessary class vote approval from preferred shareholders, making option I the correct statement.",
