      "generated_answer": "**F**\n\nThe rule of recognition, per Hart, identifies valid primary rules but does not itself confer legislative or other powers—it merely recognizes or validates existing sources of authority as ultimate. Critics find Hart's \"power-conferring\" label unconvincing because, unlike rules of change (empowering lawmakers) or adjudication (empowering judges), it functions descriptively rather than empoweringly. Option F captures this distinction precisely.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
