      "generated_answer": "**H**\n\nThe statute is unconstitutional because it interferes with the President's core Article II authority as Commander-in-Chief to direct military training and operations, including joint exercises short of hostilities. Congress's regulatory powers (Art. I, § 8) do not extend to dictating operational timelines like a mandatory three-month notice for such activities. Courts defer to presidential control over tactical military decisions absent declared war.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
