      "generated_answer": "**F**\n\nThis scenario aligns with *Ambach v. Norwick* (1979), where the Supreme Court upheld a state citizenship requirement for public school teachers under rational basis review due to their role in teaching civic values. Strict scrutiny does not apply here because teaching is a government function closely tied to state interests. Options like C, G, and H incorrectly assume strict scrutiny or absolute protection for non-citizens.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
