      "generated_answer": "A. win, because the neighbor's easement to use the driveway was conveyed to the professor.\n\nThe deed created an express appurtenant easement for ingress/egress benefiting the neighbor's Lot 2 (dominant tenement), as indicated by its nature, location, and reference to \"heirs and assigns\" in the forfeiture clause. Appurtenant easements automatically transfer with conveyance of the dominant estate (Lot 2 to professor), even without mention in the deed. Non-recording, non-use, and inheritance do not defeat the easement.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
