      "generated_answer": "**H**\n\nThe state's interpretation prohibiting stickers burdens the candidate's core political speech and expression in campaigning, including distributing materials to facilitate voters' choices, warranting strict scrutiny under the First Amendment. Other options fail because they rely on weaker equal protection claims (lacking suspect classification or intent), misapply voting rights amendments (not race, sex, poll tax, or literacy tests), or invoke non-constitutional laws. Election regulations on ballot markings trigger Anderson-Burdick balancing, but banning this expressive aid likely fails as overbroad.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
