    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1365",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hume's attack on natural law is founded on his argument that:\n\nOptions: \nA. We cannot objectively know what is morally right or wrong.\nB. Natural law is backward-looking.\nC. There is no such thing as a social contract.\nD. Natural law fails to protect the state against attacks.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
