      "generated_answer": "**B**\n\nState taxpayers generally lack standing to challenge state expenditures under the Establishment Clause absent a particularized injury beyond generalized grievance, as affirmed in cases like *Valley Forge Christian College v. Americans United* and state analogs denying such suits. The plaintiffs' status as avowed atheists does not confer standing, as ideological opposition is insufficient. The court would dismiss without reaching the merits of the statute's validity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
