    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nThe federal legislation prohibits only interstate shipment and sale of the pies, with no express preemption of state laws on intrastate commerce. States retain police power to regulate purely intrastate activities like shipment and sale within their borders, absent preemption or conflict. No implied preemption or conflict exists here, as the state statute addresses intrastate matters.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
