      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nThe Supreme Court in *Foley v. Connelie* (1978) upheld a citizenship requirement for state troopers under rational basis review, as police exercise broad discretionary powers akin to government functions, distinguishing it from broader civil service exclusions struck down in cases like *Sugarman v. Dougall*. Option A precisely matches this reasoning, while others either misstate the level of scrutiny (e.g., B, treating it as suspect) or rely on incorrect grounds (e.g., C's vague state authority, H's inapplicable Fifth Amendment).  \n\\boxed{A}",
