      "generated_answer": "**I**\n\nThe Contracts Clause prohibits states from impairing the obligation of *existing* contracts, but the woman has no prior contract with any ski resort that is being affected. The law regulates future employment licensing and does not retroactively alter any contractual obligations she holds. Options like A, B, E, F, and G fail because they misapply other doctrines (e.g., substantive due process or rational basis review) or ignore the existing-contract requirement.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
