      "generated_answer": "**C**\n\nThe oral modification increasing the quantity to 15,000 boxes is subject to UCC § 2-209(3), which requires compliance with the Statute of Frauds (UCC § 2-201) for contracts over $500 involving goods, necessitating a writing with quantity terms that is absent here. Thus, it is unenforceable due to the Statute of Frauds. Other options fail: e.g., parol evidence (J) applies to prior/contemporaneous terms, not subsequent modifications; UCC modifications need no consideration (eliminating B/E), but SOF still governs.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
