      "generated_answer": "A\n\nThe strongest constitutional argument is the Supremacy Clause (A), as the proposed state postal service directly conflicts with federal laws establishing the USPS monopoly on mail carriage (e.g., Private Express Statutes, 39 U.S.C. §§ 601–606), preempting state action. Option I invokes an exclusive federal power theory but is weaker, as Supremacy Clause preemption applies directly given Congress's legislation. Other options misapply amendments, clauses, or facts (e.g., B reverses the Tenth Amendment's effect; F ignores the distinct postal power and intrastate limit).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
