      "generated_answer": "**G**\n\nThe state's highest court upheld the statute's constitutionality based on the existing conviction, but if the trooper demonstrates the conviction was overturned on appeal, the statutory basis for denying benefits disappears entirely, allowing pension reinstatement. Other options either contradict the statute's plain language (A, B, F), fail as separate constitutional claims unlikely to succeed post-upholding (C, D, I), or lack legal efficacy (E, H).  \n\\boxed{G}",
