      "generated_answer": "B\n\nThe proposed federal law directly conflicts with certain state laws by forbidding states from compelling journalists to reveal sources in civil suits, and the Supremacy Clause (Article VI) makes valid acts of Congress the supreme law of the land, preempting contrary state laws. Options A and C suggest possible bases for congressional authority but do not directly address preemption, while D is irrelevant. Although congressional authority must exist for preemption to apply, B provides the strongest argument for why the federal law would override state laws.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
