      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nNo assault or battery because the boy lacked intent to cause apprehension of contact or any contact itself (arrow missed; injury from tree limb after reflexive duck). Negligence is plausible but not listed alone in options; E accurately excludes the intentional torts without erroneously including them as in A/D. Precautions (hay bales) and accidental loss of balance make negligence arguable but not definitive success.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
