    "prediction": "gpt-5-nano",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let E(r,b) be the maximum expected number of correct guesses with r red and b black cards remaining. If r > b, the optimal step is to guess red, giving E(r,b) = (r/(r+b))(1+E(r-1,b)) + (b/(r+b))E(r,b-1); if r < b, by symmetry E(r,b) = (b/(r+b))(1+E(r,b-1)) + (r/(r+b))E(r-1,b); if r = b, E(r,r) = 1/2(1+E(r-1,r)) + 1/2 E(r,r-1); with base E(0,b)=b and E(r,0)=r. Computing gives E(1,1)=3/2, E(2,1)=7/3, E(2,2)=17/6, E(3,1)=13/4, E(3,2)=18/5, hence E(3,3)=41/10.\n\nThus the expected number of correct guesses is 41/10, so m+n = 41+10 = \\boxed{51}.",
