      "generated_answer": "The equation \\(12x^2 - xy - 6y^2 = 0\\) implies \\(x/y = 3/4\\) or \\(x/y = -2/3\\) for \\(y \\neq 0\\), with the solution \\((0,0)\\) when \\(y = 0\\).\n\nThus, the integer solutions are \\((x, y) = (3k, 4k)\\) for integer \\(k\\) with \\(|4k| \\leq 100\\) (so \\(|k| \\leq 25\\), giving 51 pairs) and \\((x, y) = (-2m, 3m)\\) for integer \\(m\\) with \\(|3m| \\leq 100\\) (so \\(|m| \\leq 33\\), giving 67 pairs), with only \\((0,0)\\) counted twice.\n\nThe total number of ordered pairs is \\(51 + 67 - 1 = 117\\).\n\n\\boxed{117}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe provided answer derives from solving the quadratic equation \\(12x^2 - xy - 6y^2 = 0\\). Treating it as a quadratic in \\(x\\), the discriminant is \\(y^2 + 288y^2 = 289y^2 = (17y)^2\\), yielding solutions \\(x = \\frac{y \\pm 17|y|}{24}\\), or equivalently, by setting \\(t = x/y\\), the ratios \\(t = 3/4\\) or \\(t = -2/3\\) for \\(y \\neq 0\\), plus the case \\((0,0)\\).\n\nThis gives two families of integer solutions: \\((x, y) = (3k, 4k)\\) where \\(|4k| \\leq 100\\) (so \\(k\\) ranges from \\(-25\\) to \\(25\\), yielding 51 pairs) and \\((x, y) = (-2m, 3m)\\) where \\(|3m| \\leq 100\\) (so \\(m\\) ranges from \\(-33\\) to \\(33\\), yielding 67 pairs).\n\nThe pairs overlap only at \\((0,0)\\), so the total is \\(51 + 67 - 1 = 117\\).",
