      "generated_answer": "The common problem for linear genomes is the end-replication problem, where the 5' ends cannot be fully replicated due to primer removal and 5'-3' synthesis directionality. Reverse transcription in retroviruses elegantly solves this by generating complete long terminal repeats (LTRs, which are repeated sequences) at both ends of the proviral DNA through template switching. Option I best matches this definition and solution.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
