    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3322",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An actress with O type blood accused a producer with B type blood of being the father of her child in a paternity suit. The child was also O type. What does the blood type suggest about his guilt?\n\nOptions: \nA. He cannot be the father\nB. The child's blood type suggests the mother has been unfaithful\nC. The child's blood type suggests a mutation occurred\nD. He could have been the father but it does not prove it\nE. The blood type proves he is the father because O type is recessive\nF. He definitely is the father\nG. He must have been the father because B type blood can produce O type offspring\nH. The blood type does not suggest anything\nI. The child's O type blood proves his innocence\nJ. He is probably not the father because B type blood cannot produce O type offspring\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**D**\n\nBlood type O requires OO genotype; the O mother contributes O, so the child needs O from the father. A B-type father (possible BO genotype) could contribute O, making paternity possible. However, it neither proves nor excludes him as the father.\n\n\\boxed{D}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process begins by recalling ABO blood type genetics: type O requires OO genotype, type B can be BB or BO. The mother, with O blood (OO), contributes an O allele to the child, who also has O blood (OO) and thus requires an O allele from the father. A B-type father with BO genotype could contribute O, allowing for an OO child, while BB would produce a B-type child (BO). Therefore, the blood types indicate paternity is possible but not proven, as the father's exact genotype is unknown. Among the options, D accurately reflects this by stating he could be the father without proof, eliminating exclusions like A or I and overstatements like F or G.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 228,
        "output_tokens": 202,
