    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3989",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Show that l'Hôpital's rule amounts to forming a Taylor expansion of both the numerator and the denominator. Evaluate the limit\n$$\n\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 0}} \\frac{{\\ln (1+x)-x}}{{x^2}}\n$$\nboth ways.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3/2\nB. 0\nC. -3/2\nD. 2\nE. 1/4\nF. 1\nG. -1\nH.  -1/2\nI. 1/2\nJ. -2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Using Taylor expansion, \\(\\ln(1+x) = x - \\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\), so numerator is \\(-\\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\) and \\(\\frac{\\ln(1+x)-x}{x^2} = -\\frac{1}{2} + O(x) \\to -\\frac{1}{2}\\).  \nBy l'Hôpital's rule (0/0 form), differentiate to get \\(\\lim_{x\\to 0} \\frac{\\frac{-x}{1+x}}{2x} = \\lim_{x\\to 0} \\frac{-1}{2(1+x)} = -\\frac{1}{2}\\).  \nBoth methods agree, as l'Hôpital captures the leading Taylor terms.\n\n\\boxed{H}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by evaluating the limit using Taylor expansion of \\(\\ln(1+x)\\) around \\(x=0\\), which is \\(x - \\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\). Substituting yields numerator \\(\\ln(1+x) - x = -\\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\), so \\(\\frac{\\ln(1+x)-x}{x^2} = -\\frac{1}{2} + O(x)\\), and the limit as \\(x \\to 0\\) is \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\).  \n\nNext, l'Hôpital's rule applies due to the 0/0 indeterminate form: differentiate numerator to \\(\\frac{1}{1+x} - 1 = \\frac{-x}{1+x}\\) and denominator to \\(2x\\), giving \\(\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{-x/(1+x)}{2x} = \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{-1}{2(1+x)} = -\\frac{1}{2}\\).  \n\nBoth approaches match, demonstrating that l'Hôpital's rule effectively uses the first non-zero Taylor terms of numerator and denominator, confirming the limit value corresponds to option H.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 171,
        "output_tokens": 422,
        "total_tokens": 1002
      },
      "provider": "azure",
      "error": null
