    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3622",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous acid, HNO2, has a pKa value of 3.3. If a solution of nitrous acid is found to have a pH of 4.2, what can be said about the concentration of the conjugate acid/base pair found in solution?\n\nOptions: \nA. [HNO2] > [NO2-]\nB. [H2NO2+] < [NO2-]\nC. [NO2-] < [H2NO2+]\nD. [H2NO2+] > [NO2-]\nE. [NO2-] > [HNO2]\nF. [NO2-] = [HNO2]\nG. [H2NO2+] > [HNO2]\nH. [HNO2] = [H2NO2+]\nI. [HNO2] > [H2NO2+]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nFor the weak acid HNO₂ (pKₐ = 3.3), the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation gives pH = pKₐ + log([NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂]). At pH = 4.2, log([NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂]) = 0.9, so [NO₂⁻] > [HNO₂]. Species like H₂NO₂⁺ are irrelevant here.\n\n\\boxed{E}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by identifying nitrous acid (HNO₂) as a weak acid with the dissociation HNO₂ ⇌ H⁺ + NO₂⁻, where HNO₂ is the conjugate acid and NO₂⁻ is the conjugate base. Given pH = 4.2 > pKₐ = 3.3, the solution favors the deprotonated form. Applying the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation, pH = pKₐ + log([NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂]), yields 4.2 = 3.3 + log([NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂]), so log([NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂]) = 0.9, meaning [NO₂⁻]/[HNO₂] ≈ 8, confirming [NO₂⁻] > [HNO₂], which matches option E. Options involving H₂NO₂⁺ (e.g., B, C, D, G, H, I) are dismissed as it is the protonated form of HNO₂, irrelevant in aqueous solution at this pH. Other options like A ([HNO₂] > [NO₂⁻]) apply only if pH < pKₐ, and F requires pH = pKₐ.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 235,
        "output_tokens": 373,
        "total_tokens": 1325
      },
      "provider": "azure",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.0002335,
    "accuracy": 1.0
  },
