      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe mechanism consists of two steps: NO2 + F2 → NO2F + F (slow) and F + NO2 → NO2F (fast). The overall reaction is obtained by adding the steps and canceling the F intermediate, yielding 2 NO2 + F2 → 2 NO2F. The slow step is rate-determining, so its rate law is rate = k [NO2][F2], indicating first order in NO2, first order in F2, and overall second order. Among the options, B (\"Second order\") matches the overall order of the reaction.",
