      "generated_answer": "**I**\n\nThe curves intersect when \\(\\sin x = 0\\) or \\(\\cos x = 0\\), so the smallest positive \\(a = \\pi/2\\).  \nThe difference is \\((\\sin x + \\cos x)^4 - (\\sin x - \\cos x)^4 = 4 \\sin 2x \\geq 0\\) on \\([0, \\pi/2]\\).  \nArea = \\(\\int_0^{\\pi/2} 4 \\sin 2x \\, dx = 4\\).\n\n\\boxed{I}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe curves intersect where \\((\\sin x + \\cos x)^4 = (\\sin x - \\cos x)^4\\), which occurs when \\(\\sin x = 0\\) or \\(\\cos x = 0\\). The smallest positive \\(x > 0\\) is \\(x = \\pi/2\\), so \\(a = \\pi/2\\).\n\nLet \\(A = \\sin x + \\cos x\\) and \\(B = \\sin x - \\cos x\\). Then, \\(A^4 - B^4 = (A^2 + B^2)(A + B)(A - B)\\), where \\(A^2 + B^2 = 2\\), \\(A + B = 2 \\sin x\\), and \\(A - B = 2 \\cos x\\). Thus, \\(A^4 - B^4 = 2 \\cdot (2 \\sin x) \\cdot (2 \\cos x) = 8 \\sin x \\cos x = 4 \\sin 2x\\).\n\nOn \\([0, \\pi/2]\\), \\(\\sin 2x \\geq 0\\), so the area is \\(\\int_0^{\\pi/2} 4 \\sin 2x \\, dx = 4 \\cdot [-\\frac{1}{2} \\cos 2x]_0^{\\pi/2} = -2 [\\cos \\pi - \\cos 0] = -2 [-1 - 1] = 4\\).",
