      "generated_answer": "**I**\n\nBy Stokes' theorem, $\\int_S (\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{A}) \\cdot d\\mathbf{a} = \\oint_C \\mathbf{A} \\cdot d\\mathbf{r}$, where $C$ is the unit circle $x^2 + y^2 = 1$, $z=0$, parametrized by $x=\\cos\\theta$, $y=\\sin\\theta$, $\\theta \\in [0, 2\\pi]$. Then $\\mathbf{A} \\cdot d\\mathbf{r} = -\\sin^2\\theta \\, d\\theta$, and $\\int_0^{2\\pi} -\\sin^2\\theta \\, d\\theta = -\\pi$. Direct computation of the curl $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{A} = ( -1, -1, -1 )$ and flux over the projection confirms the result.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
