      "generated_answer": "**J**\n\nA high voltage battery with no resistors provides the highest voltage (V) and the lowest resistance (R = 0), maximizing current via I = V/R. Configurations with resistors (even in parallel) increase R, reducing current compared to no resistors. Among no-resistor options, high voltage exceeds low voltage (H).  \n\\boxed{J}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by applying Ohm's Law, I = V / R, where maximizing current requires the highest voltage and lowest resistance. No resistors result in the minimum resistance (R = 0), producing the greatest current among all options. Option J combines a high voltage battery with no resistors, outperforming others: it exceeds H (low voltage, no resistors) due to higher V, and surpasses resistor-inclusive options (e.g., A, I) where R > 0 reduces current regardless of voltage or arrangement.",
