    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nThe observed K$_\\alpha$ wavelengths match known values: molybdenum (Z=42) at $\\approx$0.709 Å and nickel (Z=28) at $\\approx$1.658 Å, compared to copper (Z=29) at 1.541 Å. Other options do not pair elements with these precise wavelengths (e.g., zinc K$_\\alpha$$\\approx$1.44 Å, iron $\\approx$1.94 Å).  \n\\boxed{E}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning identifies impurities by matching the observed K_alpha wavelengths to known values using Moseley's law, which relates wavelength inversely to atomic number Z (shorter wavelength indicates higher Z). The 0.7092 Å line corresponds to molybdenum (Z=42, K_alpha ≈0.709 Å), while 1.6578 Å matches nickel (Z=28, K_alpha ≈1.658 Å), flanking copper's 1.5405 Å (Z=29). Among options, only E (Molybdenum and Nickel) provides this exact pair, as alternatives like D (zinc ≈1.44 Å, chromium longer) or F (iron ≈1.94 Å, zinc ≈1.44 Å) fail to align.",
