  {
    "global index": "MathQA_1650",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ram and shyam start a two - length swimming race at the same moment but from opposite ends of the pool . they swim in lanes at uniform speeds , but hardy is faster than andy . they 1 st pass at a point 18.5 m from the deep end and having completed one length each 1 is allowed to rest on the edge for exactly 45 sec . after setting off on the return length , the swimmers pass for the 2 nd time just 10.5 m from the shallow end . how long is the pool ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 65\nB. 60\nC. 55\nD. 50\nE. 45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by defining the pool length as L meters, with Ram starting at the shallow end and Shyam at the deep end, Ram faster at speed Vr and Shyam at Vs. From the first meeting 18.5 m from the deep end, the ratio r = Vr / Vs = (L - 18.5) / 18.5, so L = 18.5(r + 1). For the second meeting 10.5 m from the shallow end, Ram swims L - 10.5 m and Shyam swims 10.5 m on their return legs after resting 45 seconds each. Setting up time equations from the start of their returns leads to t2 expressions: t2 = 2a + 45 - 10.5 / Vr and t2 = r a + 45 + (10.5 r) / Vr, where a = L / Vr. Equating and simplifying yields 18.5(1 + r)(2 - r) = 10.5(1 + r), so 18.5(2 - r) = 10.5, giving r = 2 - 21/37 = 53/37. Thus, L = 18.5(53/37 + 1) = 18.5(90/37) = 45 meters, matching option E. Verification confirms distances and times align with speeds proportional to 53:37.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 193,
        "output_tokens": 304,
        "total_tokens": 3973
